  "id": "Compound::DB00379 - Gene::1555",
  "verbalization": "Mexiletine exhibits a strong binding interaction with Cyp2e1, which is a well-documented enzyme involved in the metabolism of various substrates. This binding is consistent across multiple paths, with scores indicating a significant level of confidence in the relationship. The enzyme Cyp2e1 participates in multiple metabolic activities, including the epoxygenation and monooxygenation of arachidonic acid, as well as steroid hydroxylation. These activities are all mediated by Cyp2b6, suggesting a potential pathway through which Mexiletine may influence Cyp2b6's function. The shared participation of Cyp2e1 in these metabolic processes implies that Mexiletine could modulate Cyp2b6 activity, potentially affecting the metabolism of its substrates. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between Mexiletine and Cyp2b6, highlighting the role of Cyp2e1 as a central mediator in this relationship.",
